/.clauduct-profile/
/.clauduct-status/
/output/
/.tmp/

# Session prompts and handoffs. The evidence they produced is committed -- audits,
# verdicts, the v2 documents -- but the instructions that produced it are working
# material and stay on the machine that wrote them. Deliberately not backed up:
# they are consumables, and the outputs that matter are already in the repository.
#
# The five prompts still under docs/prompts/ are there because committed evidence
# cites them by name, and HANDOFF.md's rule is that a cited file has to be present
# or the claim cannot be checked. New evidence documents must not cite a prompt --
# doing so drags it back into the public repository through that same rule.
/docs/journal/

# Markers written by live validation runs.
/clauduct-check.txt
/clauduct-agent-validation-*.txt
